ght 1.0), but it cannot substitute for the GPS measurement that limbs (b) and (c) require, so POL-NS-01 is not satisfied in full and the fee cannot be confirmed. The driver's account that he was at the bay from about 5.47 to 5.53 (counterparty statement) is noted, but POL-NS-02 reads GPS fixes, not assertions. Chat: EV-CHAT-00213 is MISSING (weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT) while trip_record.chat_message_count = 3 shows a log existed; POL-NS-04 limbs (a) and (b) cannot be run and an undecidable limb (c) is neutral, so neither the rider's 'three messages, no reply' nor the driver's 'I answered every message' can be verified and no adverse finding is built on the lost log. Fare: not defective — $6.00 is the GREATER of the TRANSPORT_HUB zone fee ($6.00) and the RYDE_X tier fee ($4.00), so it reconciles with fee_schedule.resolution_rule (difference 0.00) and POL-NS-08(d) is not engaged. Advisory: EV-ADVIS-00213-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT), so POL-NS-06's accumulation route is unavailable and nothing extends or excuses the hold. Compensation: POL-NS-07's anti-farming check does not trip — no_show_terminations_30d = 3 (below 4) and 3/107 = 2.8% (below 8%) — but no driver compensation is payable because POL-NS-01 is not satisfied in full. Under POL-GEN-02 the MISSING artifacts carry no fact and cannot lift confidence; the escalation trigger itself rests on the two independent weight-1.0 profiles, so confidence is 0.9. Open question for the reviewer: obtain the driver's device trace and the chat log, then determine whether the driver arrived within the 150 m TRANSPORT_HUB arrival radius and held at least 300 seconds, and whether the two prior same-pair disputes indicate a pattern. No referral is recorded because no clause in this policy set directs an instruction into the escalation packet on these facts."
