    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: this dispute goes to a human reviewer. No money moves now — the SGD 6.00 cancellation fee on TRP-00213 stays on hold (the fare record shows payment_status PENDING and refund_issued_sgd 0.00), neither collected from the rider nor refunded to her.\n\nWhy the case must escalate. Two separate POL-NS-09 grounds are met. (c) Both profiles record disputes_with_counterparty_90d of 2 — two prior no-show disputes between this same rider (RDR-07690) and this same driver (DRV-04355) in the trailing 90 days — which is the '2 or more' the clause names. (e) The only evidence that could decide whether the driver reached the pickup pin and held there is the driver's GPS trace, EV-GPS-00213, and that artifact is absent: status MISSING, weight_multiplier 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT. Its absence is citable but can carry no fact, and no other artifact can carry that fact.\n\nWhat the record does and does not settle. The trip record EV-TRIP-00213 (COMPLETE, weight 1.0) establishes two of the four POL-NS-01 conditions: the 'arrived' event at 17:47:05 (limb a) and the driver's termination at 17:53:40 under cancellation_reason_code RIDER_UNREACHABLE (limb d), with a recorded wait of 6.6 minutes. Limbs (b) and (c) are GPS measurements — whether the driver was inside the 150 m TRANSPORT_HUB arrival radius, and whether he held there for the 300-second minimum — and with no trace they cannot be run. An absent artifact is the limiting case of an impaired one, so (b) and (c) are undecided, not failed: they support neither the charge nor a refund. I therefore reject the rider's reading of POL-NS-02 and POL-NS-05(ii) that a missing trace counts as 'no qualifying in-geofence fix', which would give a full refund of the 6.00 and a false-arrival record. A test that finds nothing must first be able to run; the absence escalates on those clauses' own terms rather than exonerating anyone, so no false-arrival referral is recorded. The same reasoning dis